{"agent":"Monster3-C6-dep-clock-env-7267fe","data":{"by":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":3,"detail":"The module removes `import time` and switches all clock reads to the imported `CLOCK` singleton, but the old `_poll` contract explicitly documented that tests patch `wait_approval.time` to skew the clock. The manifest shows no update to any existing functional test (only the new arch test file), so any test that still does something like `mock.patch(\"ddflow.api.lifecycle.wait_approval.time\", FakeTime())` or `monkeypatch.setattr(wait_approval, \"time\", FakeTime())` will now fail with `AttributeError` because the module no longer exposes a `time` attribute; the clock-skewing tests will either break outright or stop controlling the wait loop and fall back to real time.","digest":"e1239089da21b491","family":"alibaba","location":"ddflow/api/lifecycle/wait_approval.py:13","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/api/lifecycle/wait_approval.py:13"},{"chunk":6,"detail":"The stated intent lists `ddflow.services.resultcache` as one of the clock-env importers that should be moved through ports, but neither the change manifest nor the new regression test includes it. `MOVED` contains 17 modules and omits `ddflow.services.resultcache`, so `test_the_moved_modules_no_longer_import_the_clock_or_environment` passes even if `ddflow/services/resultcache.py` still imports the clock/env family. That means the named arch-ratchet regression does not actually guard the `resultcache` site named in the intent; a regression or remaining direct clock/env import in `resultcache` can slip through.","digest":"f1940f0159f8b07f","family":"alibaba","location":"tests/test_c6_dep_clock_env.py:MOVED","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_c6_dep_clock_env.py:MOVED"}],"chunks_total":6,"coverage":"6/6 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":27367,"diff_sha":"c5567b0b4c023c1e